# Offline inference is the default unless configured; no Brev or API key required.
# Text/uploads are processed in app-server memory: your computer for a local run,
# the hosting server for a public app. Public processing is not laptop-only.
# PDF/DOCX/TXT: backend up to 5 MiB; frontend 4,000,000 bytes for Vercel limits.
# Review/edit the preview and suggested skills; manual skill entry is available.
# Optional: install Ollama, run `ollama pull qwen2.5:3b`, then set:
NJIA_AI_PROVIDER=offline
NJIA_OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
NJIA_OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:3b

# Optional hosted coaching: set NJIA_AI_PROVIDER=groq and supply your own key
# in the server environment. No Brev required. Never put the key in frontend
# code, browser storage, request bodies, screenshots, or committed files.
# Remote coaching requires opt-in; /api/plan checks use_ai/ai_consent server-side.
# Curated plans remain available without AI consent. Only allowlisted structured
# curriculum goes to Groq, never CV text, identities, country/role or demand stats.
# Missing key, request errors, rate limits, or invalid output use curated coaching.
GROQ_API_KEY=
# Official supported models: https://console.groq.com/docs/models
# Main workflow live-tested openai/gpt-oss-20b on 2026-09-27: four weeks in 2.27s.
# One observed run, not a latency/quality benchmark; account access may vary.
# Original llama-3.3-70b-versatile was unavailable in the account model list,
# so the default changed to openai/gpt-oss-20b. Keep credentials server-side.
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
# Web research (live local jobs, interview questions) uses a separate Groq model so
# token-heavy browser searches cannot exhaust the brief model's free-tier daily limit.
NJIA_SEARCH_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# Optional backup for questions, brief and practice feedback when Groq fails:
# free key from build.nvidia.com (rate-limited trial). Same model, same validation.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
NJIA_FALLBACK_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
